<p>The 1912 U.S. presidential election was contested by three major candidates. Incumbent President {% person "william-howard-taft" %}William Howard Taft{% endperson %} was renominated by the Republican Party with the support of its conservative wing. Although Taft was {% person "theodore-roosevelt" %}Theodore Roosevelt's{% endperson %} handpicked successor, his performance in office failed to satisfy Roosevelt's political supporters, including former Mandan mayor {% person "henry-waldo-coe" %}Henry Coe{% endperson %}. After Roosevelt failed to secure the Republican nomination, he called his own convention and created the Progressive Party, nicknamed the "Bull Moose Party."</p>

