<p>With the Republican Party split in the three-way race, {% person "woodrow-wilson" %}Woodrow Wilson{% endperson %} defeated both Taft and Roosevelt in the general election. Wilson became the only Democratic president elected between 1892 and 1932. It was also the last election in which a candidate who was neither a Republican nor a Democrat placed second in either the popular vote or the Electoral College.</p>
